    <!-- Privacy policy -->
    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_updated">Last updated: October 2026</string>
    <string name="privacy_intro">Kosh is a private, offline app for scanning, reading and organising documents and notes. This policy explains what the app does with your information. In short: your documents stay on your device.</string>
    <string name="privacy_h_collect">What Kosh collects</string>
    <string name="privacy_b_collect">Kosh does not collect, upload or sell any personal information. It has no account, no analytics, no advertising and no tracking. The app does not ask for the internet permission, so it cannot send your files or notes anywhere.</string>
    <string name="privacy_h_storage">What is stored on your device</string>
    <string name="privacy_b_storage">Scanner: photos you take or import are kept in the app\'s private storage as temporary drafts until you create a PDF or discard them. Finished PDFs are saved where you choose, and a list of recent scans is kept. Reader: your reading position, bookmarks and annotations are stored on the device; the original PDF is never changed. Notes: your notes and any images you attach are stored in the app\'s private storage. Settings: your theme and tab preferences.</string>
    <string name="privacy_h_permissions">Permissions</string>
    <string name="privacy_b_permissions">Camera: used only when you open the scanner camera, to photograph pages. All files access (Android 11 and newer) or storage read access (older versions): used only to list and open the PDF files on your device in the Home tab. You can refuse these and still use the file picker to open a single PDF. You can turn either permission off in your phone\'s settings at any time.</string>
    <string name="privacy_h_sharing">Sharing and exporting</string>
    <string name="privacy_b_sharing">Kosh only shares or exports something when you choose Share, Export or Print. Files you share go to the app you pick in the Android share sheet, and that app\'s own privacy policy applies from then on. Exported files are saved in the location you select.</string>
    <string name="privacy_h_children">Children</string>
    <string name="privacy_b_children">Kosh does not knowingly collect any information from anyone, including children.</string>
    <string name="privacy_h_control">Your control</string>
    <string name="privacy_b_control">You can delete scan drafts from the Scanner tab, delete or remove any PDF, note, bookmark or annotation inside the app, and remove everything Kosh stores by clearing its storage or uninstalling it. PDFs and exports you saved elsewhere are not removed automatically.</string>
